  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 122 AM EDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nFor the middle of end of this week, enhanced jet stream dynamics \nin the western US will enhance the development of a deep trough \nout west, which in return will strengthen the ridge over the \ncentral US and an upper level trough across the Eastern Seaboard. \nAt the same time, guidance is hinting at a return in deeper \nmoisture to average or slightly above average levels. With upper- \nlevel high pressure providing some forcing for ascent along with \ndiurnal processes, rain chances will begin to increase again for \nthe end of this week and upcoming weekend. Mid-level and upper- \nlevel flow for this time period will shift to the SW as the region\nwill sit on the downstream side of the trough pattern, which will\nfavor the highest rain chances across SE Florida between 30-50%. \nUncertainty remains in how much rain could be seen, but currently\nthis setup is not anticipated to result in the type of rainfall \nwe saw this past weekend. \n\nHigh temperatures for the middle to end of this week and into next \nweekend are expected in the low to mid 80s each day, with overnight \nlows ranging from the low to mid 60s for SW Florida to the upper 60s \nand low 70s for SE Florida.",
